<!-- Copyright 2026 Life Sciences Suite Architecture Team
     License AGPL-3.0 or later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0).

     Reusable Common Technical Document section structure.

     Headings are taken from the two guidance documents named below, with the
     bracketed qualifiers of the source headings (for example
     "[name, manufacturer]" and "[name, dosage form]") removed, because those
     qualifiers are filled in per drug substance or per dosage form by the
     applicant and are not part of the fixed structure.

     Sources:
     * ICH M4(R4), reproduced by the United States Food and Drug
       Administration as "M4 Organization of the Common Technical Document for
       the Registration of Pharmaceuticals for Human Use", October 2017,
       https://www.fda.gov/files/drugs/published/M4-Organization-of-the-Common-Technical-Document-for-the-Registration-of-Pharmaceuticals-for-Human-Use-Guidance-for-Industry.pdf
       Provides: module level and sections 1.1 to 1.2, 2.1 to 2.7, 3.1 to 3.3,
       4.1 to 4.3 and 5.1 to 5.4.
     * ICH M4Q, reproduced by the United States Food and Drug Administration
       as "M4Q: The CTD, Quality", August 2001,
       https://www.fda.gov/media/71581/download
       Provides: sub-sections of 2.3 and of 3.2.

     Sub-sections of 2.6, 2.7, 4.2 and 5.3 are deliberately not shipped. Their
     headings are defined in ICH M4S and ICH M4E, which were not consulted
     when this file was written, and the two documents that were consulted do
     not agree on the number of sub-sections of 2.7 (the granularity table of
     M4(R4) shows six, M4Q lists five titles). Numbering those titles would be
     a guess. A manufacturer adds them as configuration.

     Module 1 is region specific. ICH M4(R4) states that its content and
     format can be specified by the relevant regulatory authority, so only the
     two headings given by the guidance are shipped. -->
